Implemented Components
1. Document Managing

The document-managing module is responsible for loading and processing construction-material documents.

Current functionality includes:

Loading PDF documents using PyPDFLoader

Splitting documents into smaller chunks

Using RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter

Creating overlapping text chunks for better retrieval

Current chunking configuration:

chunk_size = 452
chunk_overlap = 52
2. Vector Store — Typesense

The project uses Typesense as the vector database.

The vector-store module performs the following tasks:

Generates embeddings for document chunks

Uses Hugging Face embeddings

Stores document vectors in Typesense

Creates a searchable vector database

Retrieves relevant documents based on semantic similarity

Embedding model:

sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2

The embedding dimension is:384

3. Prompt Templates

The prompt-template module contains the prompts used by the application.

These templates define:

How the LLM should answer construction-material questions

How retrieved context should be used

How the model should avoid generating unsupported information

How individual retrieved sentences can be evaluated for relevance

The main answering prompt instructs the LLM to answer using the retrieved context and to avoid making up information.

4. LLM Model

The LLM module is responsible for configuring the language model used in the RAG pipeline.

The project currently uses:

ChatGroq

Model: openai/gpt-oss-120b

Temperature: 0

The LLM is used to generate answers based on the retrieved construction-material information.

5. Knowledge Refinement

The knowledge-refinement module is being developed as part of the Corrective RAG workflow.

The current planned workflow is:

User Question
      ↓
Retrieve Relevant Documents
      ↓
Combine Retrieved Documents
      ↓
Split Context into Sentences
      ↓
Evaluate Each Sentence for Relevance
      ↓
Keep Relevant Sentences
      ↓
Create Refined Context
      ↓
Generate Final Answer

The purpose of knowledge refinement is to remove irrelevant information from the retrieved context before sending it to the main answering LLM.

